{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_CanIf_00068","versions":[{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_CanIf_00068","release":"R19-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_CanIf_00068@rel:R20-11#8a325c7b","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_CanIf_00068","release":"R20-11","content":"[SWS_CanIf_00068] If the function CanIf_Transmit() is called\nand if the CanIf has to store the L-PDU in the transmit L-PDU\nbuffer, then if the corresponding CanIfTxBuffer is already filled,\nthe CanIf shall overwrite the older L-PDU with the recent L-PDU.\nReaction\nN/A\nReport\nThe error is either reported by the return code of CanIf_Transmit() or\nindirectly by the lack or transmission confirmation afterwards.\nRecovery\nN/A\nSee also the COM TX Deadline Monitoring, which provide a mechanism to detect\nand react (from SWC) in case of such an error.\nThis error may also impact a TP (Transport Protocol) communication; in that case,\nthis will be detected as a CAN Transport Protocol error during transmission.\nDescription of the AUTOSAR standard errors","meta":{"source_pdf":"ErrorDescription.pdf","source_page":22,"trigger_kind":"snippet_ingest"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-04T00:00:00+00:00","text_key":"9af893615aab","rejoin":{"rule":"text-rejoin@1","e":[[60,1," "],[122,1," "],[189,1," "],[254,1," "],[263,1," "],[267,1," "],[274,1," "],[345,1," "],[409,1," "],[418,1," "],[422,1," "],[499,1," "],[546,1," "],[628,1," "],[705,1," "]]}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_CanIf_00068","release":"R21-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_CanIf_00068","release":"R22-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_CanIf_00068","release":"R23-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"clas